---
import "../styles/global.css";

interface Props {
  title: string;
}
const { title } = Astro.props;
---

<html lang="es">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
    <title>{title} · Agenda</title>
  </head>
  <body class="min-h-dvh bg-paper-soft font-body text-ink antialiased">
<!--
THESIS: The day-planner page you already trust to hold your life holds
your tasks instead — a due date is today's page, not metadata.
OWN-WORLD: A cream planner page (#f5f1e6) bordered like a sheet laid on
the desk (#efe8d6), near-black ink (#1f1c18), hairline rules only
between ledger rows (#d8cfb8) — never a decorative background grid —
one date-red accent (#b5352a) spent only on today/overdue. Workhorse
system sans for text, tabular ui-monospace for every date and time
numeral. Planner-tab navigation. State is shown as a written mark — a
tick, a strike — never a second color.
STORY: Opening the app opens today's page: overdue jumps out in red,
what's next reads at a glance, adding a task is writing a new ruled
line, completing one is ticking it off.
FIRST VIEWPORT: Planner tab strip (Hoy / Todas) top; huge tabular date
heading below; a blank ruled "add a task" entry line; an OVERDUE ledger
block in accent red when any exist; a ruled list of what's due next,
sorted by date_limit.
FORM: The Day Planner Grid — IMPECCABLE'S PICK on the direction round
(assigned candidate: Courier Tracking Slip), seed key e9ceb541.
FINISH: unreviewed and undocumented is unfinished; this build ends with
the finish review, the verdict, DESIGN.md, and every shipping raster
carrying its provenance.
-->
    <div
      class="mx-auto min-h-dvh max-w-2xl border-paper-line bg-paper sm:my-8 sm:min-h-0 sm:border-x sm:border-y"
    >
      <slot />
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
